#Network/Message transfer directories
#Anchored with a leading slash on purpose. Unanchored, `files/` matches a
#directory of that name at ANY depth, so it also ignored src/views/files/ and
#src/views/qwk/. The views already committed stayed tracked, since an ignore
#rule does not touch a tracked file, so the only symptom was that a NEW view
#added under either directory was silently left out of every commit.
/qwk/
/ftn/
/qnet/

#potential file store, and the upload staging inside it
/files/
/tmp/

#Test scratch output
tests/tmp/

# TypeScript v1 declaration files
typings/

